 "config_sha256": "43ee08b659ec1d28b952900f9cca8c89dcd4f85210cba894c4eca6d0dffe16da",
 "confounds": [
  "Downscale is cv2 INTER_AREA; production decodes 160x90 with ffmpeg bicubic.",
  "Positives are synthetic blur on good windows; no real-world defocus footage was labelled.",
  "The IndEgo-only eval split has 3 clips, so its group interval is fragile; the per-dataset catch rates differ a lot (IndEgo 100% vs OOD-160 46% at sigma=3) and are therefore reported separately.",
  "IndEgo is 10 fps and is frame-repeated to 30 fps exactly as the portal does; OOD-160 is 30 fps native.",
  "lapvar_cal divides by the mean luma, so it stays PROPORTIONAL to gain (raw Laplacian variance scales with gain^2).  It is not gain-invariant: the dark control shows that a x0.5 darkening of a sharp good window can trip the rule -- the residual weakness of this statistic, reported, not hidden.",
  "One pooled threshold across two heterogeneous datasets: the per-dataset 2% clean quantiles were 0.0281 (IndEgo) and 0.0184 (OOD-160), so per-dataset operating points are an open alternative that was not shipped.",
  "The shipped-head arm runs 16 windows (8 IndEgo + 8 OOD, eval split) because the full 26-feature path costs ~0.4 s/window; its rates have n=16."
 ],
